{"skill":{"slug":"file-organizer-skill","displayName":"File Organizer Skill"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770938794313,"changelog":"- Initial release of the File Organizer skill.\n- Organize files by extension (default) or by date (year/month).\n- Supports dry run mode to preview changes without moving files.\n- Includes recursive scanning and undo functionality.\n- Tracks actions in an organize_history.json file for audit and undo.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1085,"sha256":"aae6ec1f0e20598db30f82ccc3ba702562f708ddbae84e7068718d0cc86d0178","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/categories.md","size":651,"sha256":"2d3bc5418dcb54eb65fb817f58859ab3b5ac8325d8024491bf14352bbe8e4c7a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/organize.py","size":5901,"sha256":"7057294fe7dfcad7ccd075926ef92e641e4a89803e103b3d8e5e621f0be24599","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1863,"sha256":"fcd3996a1f9c87912547c8a9ff61e0b87a218ab824b9df5512c00e92626e4628","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789064313330,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"526352bd6c3bdb3a41c0dc282c9a4d66f165755ce782c9b3d95199a0695ebcdb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/526352bd6c3bdb3a41c0dc282c9a4d66f165755ce782c9b3d95199a0695ebcdb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: file-organizer-skill\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe `scripts/organize.py` skill is suspicious due to a critical file movement vulnerability in its `undo` functionality. The `undo` function takes a user-supplied `log_file` path without sufficient validation. This `log_file` is parsed as JSON, and its `src` and `dst` fields are directly used in `shutil.move(dst, src)`. An attacker could craft a malicious `organize_history.json` file containing arbitrary `src` and `dst` paths, allowing them to move any file on the system (e.g., `/etc/passwd` to `/tmp/backup` or vice-versa) by executing the skill with the `--undo` flag, leading to potential data tampering, denial of service, or privilege escalation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163594821},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":32,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789064313330},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a disclosed local file organizer, but its undo mode can move arbitrary files based on an untrusted history JSON file.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Moving files is expected for this skill, but the undo implementation can relocate any file accessible to the running user if given a crafted history file, which is broader than the documented folder-scoped workflow.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact is a simple skill with Markdown instructions, one local Python script, and one reference file; no package install, remote retrieval, or dependency setup was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The normal organize path is user-directed, but undo accepts any log file path and replays src/dst entries without validating that the file was generated by this tool or that paths stay within the organized directory.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No services, hooks, scheduled tasks, credential access, or network behavior were found; the only persistence is an organize_history.json audit file, which undo deletes after running.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The core capability matches the stated purpose: it sorts files by extension or date, supports dry run, recursion, conflict renaming, history logging, and undo.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a local script that moves files. Use dry-run first, run it only on directories you explicitly choose, avoid recursive mode on broad folders, and do not use --undo with a history file you did not create and inspect.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The file read/write behavior is expected for a file organizer and is disclosed at a high level, but the manifest does not express an enforceable scope boundary.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Confirmed in artifact/scripts/organize.py: undo loads arbitrary JSON and passes its src/dst values directly to shutil.move without path or provenance validation.\n[SQP-2] expected: Confirmed: undo removes the supplied history file after processing. Cleanup is related to undo, but the deletion is not clearly called out in the user-facing instructions.\n[T09] unexpected: The static finding is supported by the same undo code path: unvalidated history entries can cause unintended file relocation and the log is deleted afterward.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789064313330}}}}}